+This book's title is one such pun, built in homage to the device this chapter teaches: say it aloud, and _MEAT The Bible's Symbolic Language_ is also _meet the Bible's symbolic language_ — the food and the invitation in one sound, divided only by where the speaker pauses.
 No mark on the cover chooses for you: the title is printed unpointed, and the reader's pause does for English what the vowels do for the Hebrew letters.
 And the word the title lands on is the book's whole claim: what the Introduction poured as sym:sym-milk[milk], these chapters serve as sym:sym-meat[meat].
 
